# Create Blank application:
    npx create-expo-app@latest UserManagementApp --template blank-typescript

# Install the following dependencies
    npx expo install react-native-screens react-native-safe-area-context react-native-gesture-handler react-native-reanimated

# react-native-screens - Native screen management: 
    Improves screen navigation performance by using native screen components.

# react-native-safe-area-context - Safe screen areas:	
    Prevents content from overlapping the status bar, notch, or device navigation area.

# react-native-gesture-handler - Touch gestures: 
    Supports gestures such as swiping, dragging, and drawer opening.

# react-native-reanimated - Animations: 
    Provides smooth animations and interactions, including animated transitions.


Then install the following navigation types
# npm install @react-navigation/native 
    Core navigation functionality: NavigationContainer
# npm install @react-navigation/bottom-tabs 	
    Bottom tab navigation: Home, Users, Settings
# npm install @react-navigation/native-stack
    Stack navigation: Users → Details → New User
# npm install @react-navigation/drawer
    Drawer navigation: Dashboard, Profile, Settings
    
    
    
# Open your root package.json.
Find: "main": "expo-router/entry"
Change it to: "main": "expo/AppEntry" - This tells Expo to start from App.tsx instead of Expo Router.

# Check app.json
If you have this configuration: Remove the expo-router plugin entry because we are not using Expo Router in this project.

    "plugins": [
    "expo-router"
    ]
